From 0e3ac7915d5e2ebd4f6ad093931acdaeb8a7ab88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: engmessias <vmessiaswt@gmailcom>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:12:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(fleet): default-off TUI lifecycle hooks into the
 fleet service (b15a2-S4)

- FleetTuiHooks: best-effort adapter (never raises into the host path) over an
  injected session service; host close reasons map to closed wire codes
  (tui_shutdown -> tui_exit, everything else -> session_end).
- Single funnel instrumentation: session_lifecycle._teardown_popped_session
  notes the close in a finally (no-op unless hooks installed). The note uses a
  lazy import because bind_module re-creates split-module functions with server
  globals and never publishes imported module objects.
- Restart invalidation pinned: a fresh service rejects cursors minted before
  the restart (invalid_provenance).
- Tests: 8 passed (incl. the server-rebound runtime path); regression 208
  passed; canonical tests/tui_gateway identical to base (one pre-existing
  flaky signature test fails on base too).
